  "justification": "Rationale A makes a serious error by claiming the comment provides no clear actionable step, when authors can easily infer they need to address the raised undiscussed questions. It fails to apply the full scoring rubric by ignoring the required assessment of whether the action is vague or concrete, does not cover the evidence needed to justify a complete scoring decision, and makes an unsupported claim not grounded in the evaluation material. Rationale B correctly interprets and applies the scoring rubric: it correctly identifies the action is implicit, notes the comment gives no concrete details on how authors should implement the change, which matches the description for a score of 2. All of Rationale B's claims are grounded in the evaluated text, it covers all necessary points to justify the scoring decision, and makes no unwarranted assumptions."
